openmediavault-webtop (8.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Default PGID changed from 1000 to 100 (the OMV 'users' group).
    OMV shared folders are owned by root:users with mode 2775, so with
    the previous default the desktop could not write to the data folder
    ('/nas') because its group was not a member of 'users'. The '/config'
    folder was unaffected because the image chowns it to PUID:PGID.
    Existing installations keep their stored value; set PGID to 100 in
    the settings form to fix an affected setup.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-webtop (8.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Webtop plugin for OpenMediaVault 8.x.
    - Settings: image tag, HTTP and HTTPS ports, timezone, the config
      shared folder (mounted at /config) and an optional data shared
      folder (mounted at /nas), the web login user and password, the
      page title and the PUID/PGID.
    - The Docker Compose stack is registered in the
      openmediavault-compose plugin on save (Compose.setFile), so it
      follows the Compose plugin conventions (<compose shared
      folder>/webtop/) and shows up in the Compose web UI (Services ->
      Compose -> Files / Services) where it can also be inspected,
      edited, started and stopped. The plugin does not render the
      stack files itself.
    - The config and data folders are referenced through the Compose
      placeholder '${{ sf:"<name>" }}', so a changed shared folder path
      is resolved by the Compose plugin on deploy.
    - Start/Stop/Restart/Upgrade run as background tasks (through the
      Compose plugin helper omv-compose-run) with live output.
    - Live status: container state, the resolved stack file location,
      log viewer and rendered compose file preview, plus a button to
      open the web desktop over HTTPS.
    - The container is never modified; the desktop and its
      applications are managed from within the Webtop web interface.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
